  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Drinfeld twist for quantum su(2) in the adjoint representation — We give a detailed description of the adjoint representation of Drinfeld’s twist element, as well as of its coproduct, for suq(2).\n\n**Drinfeld twist for quantum su(2) in the adjoint representation**\n\n*Chryssomalis Chryssomalakos∗*\n\n11 pp, 15 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We give a detailed description of the adjoint representation of Drinfeld’s twist element, as well as of its coproduct, for suq(2). We also discuss, as applications, the computation of the universal R-matrix in this representation and the problem of symmetrization of identical-particle states with quantum su(2) symmetry. ∗e-mail address: chryss@stp.dias.ie\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 2 Quantum su(2) in the adjoint representation; 2.1 The factorized basis; 2.2 The reduced basis; 3 The Drinfeld-Kohno theorem; 4 Adjoint representation of the twist; 4.1 Preliminaries; 4.2 Explicit computation of Fq; 5 Applications; 4.3 The representation of the coproduct of F; 5.1 The universal R-matrix in the adjoint repr; 5.2 Quantum symmetrization; References; Appendix",
      "lang": "en",
